	METHOD aR canActIndependently ()Z
		COMMENT True when this unit may act on its own current waypoint: its attachment slot (if any) does not forbid autonomous behaviour, and it accepts orders. Base implementation: getAttachmentSlot() == null || !slot.O, then && canReceiveOrders(). Consulted by processMoveWaypoint/processBuildWaypoint/processAttackWaypoint/processRepairReclaimWaypoint to decide whether to keep executing the waypoint or pop it, and by InterfaceEngine.handleBuildingPlacement and BattleInterface.getUnitInfoStatsText. CustomUnit additionally returns false when the ini flag dP is set.
	METHOD as getNextWaypoint ()Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/au;
	METHOD aS canAttackIndependently ()Z
		COMMENT Whether this unit may freely acquire/engage targets on its own. Base implementation just delegates to canActIndependently(); CustomUnit narrows it to non-buildings whose attachment slot does not forbid it. Read by AI.c(OrderableUnit) when picking targets, InterfaceEngine.hasSelectedUnitsWithWeapon (attack cursor), InterfaceEngine.update and BattleInterface.handleDragSelection/getSpecialActionsForSelection.
