	METHOD ba getMoveYAxisScaleReciprocal ()F
		COMMENT Reciprocal of the y-axis movement scaling, applied before the facing angle is computed. CustomUnit returns this.meta.ek, which CustomUnitMetadataLoader computes as 1.0F / [movement]moveYAxisScaling (and throws if that key is <= 0). Sole caller is updateMoveThrottle, which rescales the target's y coordinate as "(var8 - this.ep) * this.ba() + this.ep" before passing it to CommonUtils.angleBetweenPoints, so a unit that visually moves slower/faster along y still turns toward the visually correct point. The forward scaling itself is exposed separately as getMoveYAxisScaling().
